Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2D): resolve virtual mixed-
filament IDs at the LayerRegion level so per-region flow + extruder
decisions land on the right physical filament/nozzle.

Without this, a print authored with `wall_filament=5` (a virtual
mixed-filament row) goes through libslic3r's default flow path
which:
  - calls `region().extruder(role)` and gets the literal `5`,
  - passes `5` to `PrintConfig::nozzle_diameter.get_at(5 - 1)` which
    overflows past the 4 physical slots → falls back to default
    `0.4` nozzle even when the actual physical extruder is `0.2`,
  - computes Flow / extrusion width / gap-fill spacing from that
    wrong nozzle.

This patch adds three pieces:

1. `Layer.hpp` — declares `LayerRegion::extruder(FlowRole) const`.
   One-line addition; the method does the resolution every flow-using
   caller now goes through.

2. `LayerRegion.cpp` — three anonymous-namespace helpers
   (`effective_layer_filament_id`, `effective_infill_filament_id`,
   `use_base_infill_filament`) and the `LayerRegion::extruder()`
   implementation. The helpers consult `MixedFilamentManager` via
   `Print::mixed_filament_manager()` (the manager is populated by
   patch 0018's PrintApply hook). `use_base_infill_filament` honors
   the FS `enable_infill_filament_override` +
   `infill_filament_use_base_first_layers` /
   `infill_filament_use_base_last_layers` keys (declared in patch
   0027). `LayerRegion::flow(FlowRole, double)` is rewritten to look
   up per-role line widths directly (the FS shape; matches FS v0.9.9
   LayerRegion.cpp:107-141), and `bridging_flow` switches to
   `this->extruder(role)` so bridge flow uses the resolved nozzle.
   `make_perimeters()` builds a per-call `PrintRegionConfig` override
   with resolved wall_filament / sparse_infill_filament /
   solid_infill_filament so PerimeterGenerator emits correct
   physical IDs into per-perimeter extruder fields.

3. `Fill/Fill.cpp` — three call sites switch from
   `layerm.region().extruder(role)` to `layerm.extruder(role)` so
   the resolved physical extruder is used for infill flow / pattern
   selection. The ipLockedZag branch picks up the same `effective_extruder`
   for its skin + skeleton flow nozzle_diameter lookup.

Mechanical port from FS v0.9.9
(`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit b3c41fda),
`src/libslic3r/LayerRegion.cpp` lines 1-141 + 190-220 and
`src/libslic3r/Fill/Fill.cpp` lines 842-1083. Verified compile-clean
via full libslic3r rebuild (37/37 objects, 0 FAILED) +
:app:assembleDebug.

Hard dependency on:
  - patch 0015 (`MixedFilamentManager::effective_painted_region_filament_id`)
  - patch 0017 (`Print::mixed_filament_manager()`)
  - patch 0018 (PrintApply calls `load_custom_entries`)
  - patch 0027 (PrintRegionConfig fields enable_infill_filament_override +
    use_base_first_layers / _last_layers declared as typed members)

Soft dependency: works correctly for both LayerCycle (the prior code
path resolved via ToolOrdering only — this resolves at flow-decision
time as well, so the picked nozzle is right) and any Pointillisme /
Local-Z mode that lands later (those will reuse this resolution).

